	The BOAST-VHS program on this disk includes 2 source code files,
      4 example data input files, 1 compiled data editor file, and 1 compiled 
      executable main program file. Their names are:

	  BOASTVHS.FOR     VHSPARM.FOR     BOASTVHS.EXE    BOASTED.EXE
	  TSTPBM1.DAT      TSTPBM2.DAT     TSTPBM3.DAT     TSTEDIT.DAT

	The source files for BOASTVHS were compiled on an IBM compatible
      486DX using FORTRAN 77, Version 4.10 by Lahey Computer Systems, Inc.
      Targeting the 80286/287 instruction set.  The main source file
      "BOASTVHS.FOR" requires one INCLUDE file named, "VHSPARMS.FOR."

	In order to compile these files properly, they must reside in the 
      following path:  "D:\F77L\BOASTVHS\."  This path  may be changed by 
      modifying the INCLUDE statements in the main source code file 
      "BOASTVHS.FOR."  Also, the grid dimensions, number of wells, number 
      of PVT table entries, and other parmeters of the simulator may changed 
      by modifying the file "VHSPARM.FOR."  
	
	The interactive input data editor, BOASTED, can only edit files which 
      it creates.  BOASTED needs the special numbers found on the RECURRENT 
      DATA record line, such as found in TSTEDIT.DAT.  This file can be 
      re-edited.  The other three test case files tstpbm1, 2, & 3.dat were 
      not created by BOASTED and therefore cannot be edited by BOASTED!

	Two items not mentioned in the manual:  
	
	1) When building a grid system with non-constant values for permeability 
	   and porosity, one must enter a real non-zero value for these 
	   parameters in each cell.  If you want to exclude certain cells on 
	   the edge or any other location, set the transmissibility to zero 
	   for those cells. Assigning a value of zero for permeability and/or 
	   porosity will result in a fatal error!

	2) The maximum number of grid cells that can be run within the 640 K
	   memory limitation is 700.  If you have additional memory, larger 
	   grid systems can be run.  To do so, the file VHSPARMS.FOR must be
	   changed to reflect the number of cells one wishes.  Also, there is a
	   flag in the source code that checks the x, y, z product.  This must
	   also be changed to be consistent with or larger than the value specified
	   in the VHSPARMS.FOR file.  The source code must then be re-compiled.   
